        "rationale": "Preserves the argument, historical examples, quantities, recommendations and conditional optimism. The environmental and dystopian caveats remain explicit.",
        "quote": "Suponiendo que podamos mejorar el impacto medioambiental y evitar una pesadilla distópica."
      },
      {
        "dimension": "technicalAccuracy",
        "score": 4,
        "confidence": 0.92,
        "rationale": "The distinction between supporting learning and interrupting development is preserved. «Un mundo aumentado» is an opaque rendering of the practical integration of AI. Inherited factual assertions require separate source review.",
        "quote": "cuándo la IA amplifica el aprendizaje y cuándo cortocircuita el desarrollo"
      },
      {
        "dimension": "completeness",
        "score": 5,
        "confidence": 0.99,
        "rationale": "All substantive sections remain, including the assessment recommendation, closing jab and footnote. Dates and numerical claims are retained.",
        "quote": "**Los educadores deben rediseñar las evaluaciones**"
      },
      {
        "dimension": "readability",
        "score": 4,
        "confidence": 0.96,
        "rationale": "The opening and shorter second paragraph read naturally. A few literal constructions interrupt otherwise clear prose, particularly the GPS benefit and «mundo aumentado».",
        "quote": "ganamos la capacidad de navegar con más frecuencia"
      },
      {
        "dimension": "grammarSpelling",
        "score": 5,
        "confidence": 0.97,
        "rationale": "Agreement, accents, question punctuation and Spanish title capitalization are sound. The awkward passive constructions are stylistic issues, not grammatical failures.",
        "quote": "No, no puede replicar la inteligencia emocional ni la creatividad humanas."
      },
      {
        "dimension": "idiomMetaphor",
        "score": 4,
        "confidence": 0.96,
        "rationale": "«Se rasga las vestiduras» recreates the source's «hand-wringing» as recognizable Spanish mockery. It loses the image of anxious hands and gains a stronger suggestion of theatrical outrage; that shift fits the surrounding sarcasm. «Cortocircuita» also preserves the technical metaphor effectively.",
        "quote": "¿Quién se rasga hoy las vestiduras por la pérdida de la capacidad de leer mapas?"
      },
      {
        "dimension": "authorVoice",
        "score": 4,
        "confidence": 0.96,
        "rationale": "The dry watch joke, «idiotez», calculator provocation and impatient closing preserve the direct voice. A few abstract phrases sound more institutional than the surrounding prose. No profanity has been removed from the supplied source.",
        "quote": "No vaya a ser que tengamos que mirar un reloj de agujas."
      },
      {
        "dimension": "localeAppropriateness",
        "score": 5,
        "confidence": 0.94,
        "rationale": "The vocabulary is broadly intelligible across Spanish-speaking regions. «Agoreros» and «rasgarse las vestiduras» are literary choices rather than unexplained regional slang; they suit the satirical register.",
        "quote": "Considera el GPS: los agoreros tenían técnicamente razón."
      },
      {
        "dimension": "structureFlow",
        "score": 5,
        "confidence": 0.97,
        "rationale": "Splitting the source's long second sentence makes the example easier to follow, then returns to the historical argument. «Repasemos el historial» loses the comic receipts image in «check our historical receipts» but gains immediate clarity. The overall historical-pattern → GPS → educational-response arc remains coherent and needs no forced reordering.",
        "quote": "Antes de hiperventilar, repasemos el historial de estos pánicos."
      },
      {
        "dimension": "mdxIntegrity",
        "score": 5,
        "confidence": 0.95,
        "rationale": "The supplied text preserves emphasis, the literal footnote marker and the HTML spacer. Relative asset paths retain the same identities when resolved from the supplied es/index.mdx location. There are no executable blocks, imports, hydration directives, quizzes or external URLs to alter.",
        "quote": "cover_full_width: ../banner-thinking-decay-wide.webp"
      }
    ],
    "unresolved": [
      {
        "severity": 3,
        "claim": "«Mundo aumentado» remains an opaque calque in a central recommendation; a more explicit description would improve the practical meaning.",
        "quote": "para un mundo aumentado por la IA",
        "requiresReference": false
      },
      {
        "severity": 3,
        "claim": "The GPS benefit remains awkwardly expressed: «capacidad de navegar con más frecuencia» makes frequency sound like a capability and weakens the concrete example.",
        "quote": "ganamos la capacidad de navegar con más frecuencia",
        "requiresReference": false
      }
    ],
    "summary": "Ready under the stated threshold: readability reaches 4/5, with no identified severity-4 or deterministic hard failure. Two noticeable wording issues remain visible. The adaptation preserves the argument and dry humor; inherited factual concerns need separate source review."
  },
  "findings": [
    {
      "quote": "para un mundo aumentado por la IA",
      "sourceQuote": "for an AI-augmented world",
      "claim": "«Aumentado» suggests enlargement without clearly conveying how AI supports activity. Its abstraction weakens the paragraph's otherwise direct educational recommendation.",
      "severity": 3,
      "suggestion": "Use «para un mundo en el que usamos la IA como apoyo». This makes the source's augmentation relationship explicit; it loses the compressed label and gains clarity without adding a new prediction.",
      "evidenceIds": []
    },
    {
      "quote": "ganamos la capacidad de navegar con más frecuencia, en cualquier ciudad del mundo",
      "sourceQuote": "we gained the ability to navigate more often, in any city worldwide",
      "claim": "The literal combination «capacidad de navegar con más frecuencia» is cumbersome. In a paragraph about paper maps and city travel, «orientarnos» gives readers a more concrete action. The source itself is awkward, so the improvement should retain its frequency claim.",
      "severity": 3,
      "suggestion": "Use «Ahora podemos orientarnos más a menudo, en cualquier ciudad del mundo». This retains frequency and geographic scope while replacing the heavy capability construction with a direct verb.",
      "evidenceIds": []
    },
    {
      "quote": "Internet fue temido como el fin de la capacidad de atención",
      "sourceQuote": "The internet was once feared as the end of attention spans",
      "claim": "The passive «fue temido como» is understandable but sounds translated. Expressing what people feared produces a more natural Spanish sentence.",
      "severity": 2,
      "suggestion": "Use «Se temía que internet acabara con nuestra capacidad de atención». This preserves the feared consequence and gains a more conversational rhythm.",
      "evidenceIds": []
    }
  ],
  "sourceConcerns": [
    "«In the 1940s, educators warned that CliffsNotes would make students lazy readers» needs chronological verification. The checked packet provides no evidence about CliffsNotes history, so this assessment does not establish a corrected date. The candidate faithfully inherits the claim.",
    "«Most people under 40 can't read paper maps» is a quantified population claim without supporting evidence in the packet. «La mayoría de las personas menores de 40 años» preserves it accurately; any evidentiary repair belongs in the source.",
    "«No, it can't replicate human emotional intelligence or creativity» is a categorical claim whose scope depends on what «replicate» means. The supplied references do not establish it. The candidate preserves the assertion rather than introducing the uncertainty."
  ]
}
